It&#x27;s not enough for compactly expressing imperative logic. In Scala:<p><pre><code>  resultOption match {
    case Some(x) => println(x)
    case None => println(&quot;error&quot;)
  }
</code></pre>
Without pattern match:<p><pre><code>  if (resultOption.isDefined) {
    println(resultOption.get)
  } else {
    println(&quot;Error&quot;)
  }
</code></pre>
The .get is the problem.
